Joel Finch <jfinch@ozemail.com.au> writes:

>This is not aimed at anyone in particular, but ....
>Personally I think Hack will lose at lot of its "charm" or
>playablility if converted to a 3D first-person EOB-style 
>format.
>How can you show a map of the whole level other than with a map
>of the whole level? How would you implement all of the features
>of Hack into one easy-to-use graphical interface? I've got 
>nothing
>against 3D games, but I think you won't be able to call it Hack
>when you're finished converting it. Comments?

You could do something akin to what is done in Doom.  Doom provides an
automapping mode with the <TAB> key.  This brings up a full-screen,
nethack-like, map-as-you-go display.  Unlike Blake Stone by Apogee, you
can move around within the map and when you switch back to 3D-mode, your
position is appropriately changed.  There is even a radar set you can pick
up which functions almost the same as a scroll of magic mapping.  My only
gripes are that I don't have a dog :) and you can't see any of the aliens
(monsters) nor the weapons (treasures). 
  It is also multi-player (up to 4 with IPX packets, 2 with a serial 
cable) with cooperation or no-holds-barred.  Given the size of nethack 
already and the size of doom, I would hate to see the memory/hd requirements.
  I think the kicker would be the artwork for the 3D version.  I think it 
would take an organisation such as ID to generate a 3D version of nethack 
but of course, they won't due to the licensing restrictions.

Just my opinions,



